CPUFULL:
\paragraph{CPU}
We ran every exported model on the CPU of our environment, an Intel Xeon processor at 2.10~GHz in a virtual machine with two virtual cores.
\wosnew{For each run, we timed the fastest of three single-threaded Numba kernels (dense, sparse and bit-sliced), including input packing.
Every kernel reproduced the software reference on every test sample of all 80 runs.
Section~S5 of the supplementary material describes the kernels and the timing protocol.
The virtual machine is shared, so the standard deviations in Table~\ref{tab:cpu} include timing noise.}
The virtual machine exposes no power counters, so CPU energy was not measured.

